---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
import photo from '../assets/geoff-about.jpg';
---

<Base title="About">
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>Hey, I'm Geoff</h1>
    <p>I'm a front-end developer in Hamilton, Ontario.</p>

    <Image src={photo} alt="Geoff Jamieson" widths={[480, 960]} sizes="(min-width: 720px) 480px, 100vw" />

    <h2>Koji Street</h2>
    <p>
      I studied commerce at the University of Windsor, with a semester abroad in Sweden. After
      graduating, I founded Koji Street, a marketplace connecting artists with people who wanted to
      buy their original work. I did almost everything myself. I designed the product and the brand,
      interviewed users, ran our social media and ads, and grew it to about 250 users in six months.
    </p>
    <p>
      The one thing I didn't do was build it. An outside development team wrote the code, and
      depending on someone else to get the details right frustrated me. So I decided that whatever I
      made next, I'd be able to build myself.
    </p>

    <h2>Teaching myself to code</h2>
    <p>
      I started with freeCodeCamp and React, then went deeper into plain JavaScript, working through
      most of a book on building a front-end framework from scratch. Somewhere along the way I
      realized I really liked it. I like digging in and picking up new skills, and I like seeing the
      output of my input. I joined a Chingu team project, building a React app with four other
      people, and soon after started my first developer role.
    </p>

    <h2>LCube Studios</h2>
    <p>
      I spent two and a half years at LCube Studios, a small design and development agency. I was
      the main developer on Giving Gap, a nonprofit platform, where I rebuilt the whole website on a
      modern stack, and I built tools for other clients and for the agency itself. I picked up Vue
      and Nuxt on the job, and kept taking on more of the stack, up to shipping a full-stack AI app.
    </p>

    <h2>What I care about</h2>
    <p>
      I care about the product as much as the code, including who it's for, what problem it solves,
      and whether it's working. I want to build cool things that help people. I take ownership of
      what I build, and I document it so the next person can pick it up. I use AI every day, with my
      own judgment in charge.
    </p>
    <p>
      What I want next is a team that cares about what it's building and the people using it, where
      I can keep learning and keep building across the stack.
    </p>

    <h2>Outside of work</h2>
    <p>
      Some of the things I like doing are hiking, rock climbing, cooking,
      <a href={site.storygraph}>reading</a>, and playing old video games. I listen to a lot of
      <a href={site.bandcamp}>music</a> and collect CDs and vinyl. I also like working on fun
      coding side projects.
    </p>
    <p>
      Right now I'm building a music visualizer for fun. It's a music player for my own library,
      running on an HTTP server I'm writing from scratch in TypeScript to learn how servers work
      under the hood. Eventually it'll show visuals that react to the music, inspired by the look of
      2000s players like Winamp. It's not done yet, but it'll be up here when it is.
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
